<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70847" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νικ-ητικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>likely to conquer, conducing to victory,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				3.4.11
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπόθεσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					24.9.4
				</span></i>
			 (
				Comp.
			); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅπλον ν.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>OGI</u>
					90.39
				</span></i>
			 (Rosetta, <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ
				-ώτατον</span> the <i>most likely way to conquer,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
			</span></i><i>Comp. Phil.Flam.</i><i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eust.
					1006.28
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νικητικόν, τό,</span>
			<i>charm for victory,</i> esp. in horse-racing, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PMag.Lond.</u>
				121.390
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				1478.1
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii/iv A.D.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. δικαστηρίων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PMag.Osl.</u>
					1.35
				</span></i>
			: pl., <i>PMag.Leid. W.</i><i><span class="en">
				8.29
			</span></i>.</div>
